# The build context is this directory, and two things in it are enormous and
# never referenced by a COPY: the staged libraries and the local monero_c
# checkouts that build-darwin.sh / build-ios.sh create (.gitignore calls those
# "tens of GB of toolchain + SDK build intermediates").
#
# BuildKit transfers only files a COPY names, so for it the cost is the context
# scan rather than the bytes. The legacy builder (DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0) sends the
# whole context, and there it is the difference between a build and a wedged
# one. Excluded for both reasons.
.monero_c-*/
lib/*/

# The xip is COPYed in deliberately -- see the `COPY --chown=user:user xcode/`
# step -- so xcode/ as a whole must NOT be excluded here.
